":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT, I'd intervene on the function F_x, taking my observation as the input, with Sasha as my lead. The other copy, though, computes F_y from its own observation, Rowan's, so the question is whether its act subjunctively depends on F_x at all. By the essay's rule, that only holds if the mechanism producing its output evaluates on my input x, and it doesn't.\n\nUnder A-FDT, the other copy's output is held fixed at its prior, since its mechanism evaluates on y rather than my input x. With that fixed, defecting comes out ahead whatever q is, so I'd submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9625,"completion_tokens":648,"total_tokens":10273,"cost":0.05146,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05146,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0385,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01296},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":421,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}